\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces Development table for the main comparison under always-on protocol $R$ (mean $\pm $ std, 20 seeds; lower is better). This is a development table on station traces whose $O$ and $U$ layers are protocol-constructed, not a real-mobility ranking. Both Design settings are reported on both blocks, so the table is a within-dataset factor. WorstGroupRMSE is the maximum over the four UTC groups. On SensorScope both RAVEN settings, and on U-Air RAVEN-NoDesign, stay within the descriptive $+0.5\%$ worst-group tolerance versus those two (TEST seeds $30011$--$30020$); U-Air RAVEN-Design is outside it at $+7.9\%$ and $+8.0\%$. We do not claim a Holm-significant RMSE win. A supplemental protocol table uses intermittent occupancy.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main_effectiveness}{{III}{13}{}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Design versus No-Design, estimated and oracle propensities (20 seeds; positive $=$ Design worse). On SensorScope, Design slightly reduces $\Delta _{\mathrm  {group}}$ ($-1.23\%$ estimated, $-1.03\%$ oracle) with a flat RMSE. On U-Air, estimated and oracle Design both worsen $\Delta _{\mathrm  {group}}$ and $\mathrm  {RMSE}_{\mu }$ by about $7.5\%$. Algorithm~\ref {alg:window_close} runs RAVEN-NoDesign on U-Air; this figure diagnoses the reversal, not the selection rule. The U-Air Design-on $\Delta _{c\text  {-}s}$ gain remains in Table~\ref {tab:e4_ablation}.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
